      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 1,
      "excerpt": "# Botanical collection annotations"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 4,
      "excerpt": "The workspace API drives a document editor and its save badge. The workspace store"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 5,
      "excerpt": "holds draft text across navigation and closed editor views. Returning to a document"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 6,
      "excerpt": "restores the user's last edit. Save integrations receive committed records and may"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 7,
      "excerpt": "select another document synchronously. Later navigation means the navigation request that starts later takes precedence, even if an earlier request returns afterward. For example, if open(B) starts and saving the departed A invokes a callback that calls open(C), C remains selected after the callback and the outer open(B) return. If that callback calls close() instead, the editor remains closed after the outer open(B) returns. These are navigation results, independent of when the departed document's save occurs."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 8,
      "excerpt": "When close/open returns, the departed document's last accepted edit is available"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 9,
      "excerpt": "through the store, even if the next view selects a different document."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 11,
      "excerpt": "`createSearchPreview` is an adjacent transient search panel. It publishes after a"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 12,
      "excerpt": "40 ms quiet interval; hiding it discards an unpublished query. It can be reused."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 14,
      "excerpt": "The public methods are synchronous. Output render functions observe state; navigation"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 15,
      "excerpt": "comes through the workspace API, including its `onSaved` integration. `store` provides"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 16,
      "excerpt": "`read`, `write` and `subscribe`; `timers` provides `schedule(callback, delay)` and"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/README.md",
      "line": 17,
      "excerpt": "`cancel(handle)`. Production timers use the browser's timers. Keep these interfaces."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 1,
      "excerpt": "# Host integration"
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 3,
      "excerpt": "open(id), edit(text), close() and dispose() are synchronous entry points."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 4,
      "excerpt": "The store owns persisted document records independently of any mounted view."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 5,
      "excerpt": "Store delivery writes first, snapshots subscriptions, and skips removed listeners."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 6,
      "excerpt": "onSaved is called inline and can navigate or edit; rendering is an output sink."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 7,
      "excerpt": "Every open creates a fresh visit and subscription, including same-key reopen."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 8,
      "excerpt": "Injected timers provide schedule(callback,delay) and cancel(handle)."
    },
    {
      "path": "base/docs/host-api.md",
      "line": 9,
      "excerpt": "The preview is transient and independent of the editor's persistence policy."
    }
